      "text": "Access Control. Lost: $29k"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "FPR was exploited on BNB Chain on 14 December 2022 through improper access control, resulting in reported losses around $29,000. Four vulnerable contracts allowed arbitrary admin assignment, enabling the attacker to drain FPR tokens and LP assets. The core failure was improper access control: several contracts exposed a public setAdmin() function without access restriction. The attacker reassigned admin rights, then withdrew FPR tokens and FPR/USDT LP tokens."
